[{"artifact_id":"Figure1","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"a5672497671518d3b3d79698becfd5a4bbdc512bb02a002a473db501c3b097c8","page_index":1,"region":{"x1":72.0,"y1":74.88,"x2":540.0,"y2":335.52},"caption_region":{"x1":70.86599731445312,"y1":349.7367858886719,"x2":541.1378173828125,"y2":398.8900146484375},"caption":"Figure 1 Multi-Shot Video Extrapolation (MSVE). (a) Single-shot extrapolation extends an anchor into one continuous take but lacks cinematic structure. (b) Multi-shot storytelling imposes shot structure but does not preserve an observed anchor. (c) MSVE combines both: from v0, c, and T the system generates an adaptive shot sequence {si}ni=1 with∑ i di = T that preserves anchor state, advances the narrative, and produces plausible transitions under a finite per-call budget.","image_text":["55s","S5","18s","blue","clock-tower","destination","S4","65s","rainy","street…","S3","12s","back","repair","room","S2","35s","11:58","f…","S1","father's","engraving","v₀","OURS","Keeps:","identity","·","scene","·","objects","·","action","·","style","across","shots.","3","Multi-view,","multi-angle","dynamic","generation","Across","shots,","camera,","location","and","viewpoint","change","freely;","identity,","scene,","objects,","action","and","style","stay","consistent.","2","Single-frame","extrapolation","Anchored","to","one","observed","frame","v₀","—","the","model","continues","this","exact","world,","not","an","invented","one.","1","Adaptive","Per-shot","duration","is","decided","by","the","model,","not","a","fixed","grid","—","short","beats","stay","short","(12s),","long","beats","can","breathe","(65s).","↑","shot","·","chunk","·","segment","—","adaptive","granularity","instead","of","a","fixed","5","s","grid","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","chunk","Adaptive","shot","→","chunk","→","segment","hierarchy","shot","·","S1","shot","·","S2","shot",