ator is narrower than its nominal window. The three panels diagnose the three bottlenecks analysed in this section: (a) global planning overload, where over-detailed plans introduce unsupported constraints; (b) shot-level dilution, where longer per-shot prompts reduce the salience of state needed by the current call; and (c) temporal chaining, where generated frames become a lossy and aging memory of identity, scene, object, and action state. Additional context helps only while it raises the density of usable state. Per-panel numerical anchors are in Appendix D.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2605.26525v1-Figure2-1-1bac5d3acbc1.png","asset_sha256":"1bac5d3acbc1e771927dda9eebe5754bf843f8c3fcbc45f9aad57d0ee9c2a7cf","metadata_sha256":"c784666499ef4b66894afec001515901e4003c8ae86bf172c6fe3afaaf8e8457"},{"artifact_id":"Figure3","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"a5672497671518d3b3d79698becfd5a4bbdc512bb02a002a473db501c3b097c8","page_index":5,"region":{"x1":70.56,"y1":73.92,"x2":541.4399999999999,"y2":331.2},"caption_region":{"x1":70.62699890136719,"y1":342.9248046875,"x2":542.4146728515625,"y2":424.95599365234375},"caption":"Figure 3 Recursive Context Allocation (ReCA). (1) Recursive planning decomposes the long-video task (root) into context-bounded subproblems; only leaf nodes (blue) call the frozen generator. The induced sequence of leaves produces a variable-length Generated Video Timeline. (2) Leaf execution. Each leaf invokes one generator call and produces a video segment. (3) Leaf execution logic. Independent leaves can run concurrently as parallel segments (green); leaves that share a boundary frame are chained sequentially with handoff arrows (orange). Segment durations are adaptive to context and budget. (4) Adaptive state update. Each generated segment is read by an extractor for observation and verification, refreshes the persistent state (memory, confidence, freshness), and feeds back into planning and allocation, closing the recursion.","image_text":["→","→","→"],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2605.26525v1-Figure3-1-3a3bf3e4ec38.png","asset_sha256":"3a3bf3e4ec38c0019b31c535d09071e7c1ce64806d6a03227d41ffafb4e476c0","metadata_sha256":"c784666499ef4b66894afec001515901e4003c8ae86bf172c6fe3afaaf8e8457"},{"artifact_id":"Table1","kind":"table","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"a5672497671518d3b3d79698becfd5a4bbdc512bb02a002a473db501c3b097c8","page_index":6,"region":{"x1":72.0,"y1":148.79999999999998,"x2":540.0,"y2":328.32},"caption_region":{"x1":70.53399658203125,"y1":76.0948257446289,"x2":542.920654296875,"y2":136.2080078125},"caption":"Table 1 Quantitative Evaluation. Models are grouped by rendering backbone; methods within a block share the generator, the per-call duration budget, and the long-video prompt package, so absolute scores are comparable inside a block. Each cell reports mean± standard error over the 20 MSVE prompts. We report averaged VBench scores, NB-Q for MSVE-Bench, ViStory-Self and ViStory-Cross for single-shot and cross-frame consistency, and MovieBench for hierarchical shot alignment.The Normalisation for Avg. column carries no error bar because it aggregates six metrics with different per-cell variances; for significance use the per-metric SE columns directly.","image_text":["HappyHorse","1.0","(HappyHorse","AI,","2026)","I2V","Extension","0.948±0.009","0.961±0.012","0.539±0.029","0.158±0.019","20.214±1.37","0.102±0.026","0.485","VGoT","(Zheng","et","al.,","2024)","0.978±0.007","0.978±0.010","0.710±0.024","0.370±0.029","24.470±1.49","0.153±0.025","0.572","Mora","(Yuan","et","al.,","2024)","0.974±0.008","0.975±0.011","0.798±0.022","0.331±0.027","25.165±1.31","0.273±0.033","0.600","MovieAgent","(Wu","et","al.,","2025)","0.976±0.007","0.980±0.009","0.610±0.026","0.284±0.024","27.962±1.45","0.687±0.043","0.636","R